# Copy this file to .env.local for local development (git-ignored — see .gitignore).
# In production, set the same two variables in the Cloudflare Pages dashboard under
# Settings > Environment variables, for both the Production and Preview environments.

# Resend API key. Sign up at resend.com (free tier, no card required), then
# Dashboard > API Keys > Create API Key. Starts with "re_".
RESEND_API_KEY=

# The inbox that should receive submissions from both patient-facing forms: "Request a
# call back" (app/api/request-callback/route.ts) and "Book an appointment"
# (app/api/request-appointment/route.ts). One inbox for both to start; if LIMS wants
# them routed to different desks later, split this into two env vars and two `to`
# addresses in lib/send-notification-email.ts's two call sites — nothing else changes.
NOTIFY_EMAIL=

# Until limshisar.com is verified as a sending domain in Resend (Dashboard > Domains >
# Add Domain, then add the DNS records Resend gives you), both routes send from
# Resend's shared onboarding@resend.dev address (see lib/send-notification-email.ts).
# In that unverified state Resend will only deliver mail to the email address on the
# Resend account itself — so NOTIFY_EMAIL must be that same address for a local/staging
# test to actually arrive. Once the domain is verified, update the `from` address in
# lib/send-notification-email.ts to a limshisar.com address and NOTIFY_EMAIL can point
# anywhere.
